From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: awlx <6527744+awlx@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 13:44:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] build: drop site negations that only cancel feature packages

With apk (OpenWrt 25.12) each "-pkg" entry of a device goes into one
"apk del" call when the image is made. If a site negates a package
that only a feature selects, this package is never built. Then
"apk del" stops with "No such package" and removes nothing. On
devices that change kmod-ath10k-ct to kmod-ath10k (ipq40xx-generic),
the "apk add" then fails because both packages own the same files.

A site negation that cancels a feature package now only removes the
package from the selection. It does not go into the removal list.
---
 scripts/target_config_lib.lua | 14 ++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/scripts/target_config_lib.lua b/scripts/target_config_lib.lua
index adf58a6e1498..347e5b7d0a15 100644
--- a/scripts/target_config_lib.lua
+++ b/scripts/target_config_lib.lua
@@ -127,8 +127,18 @@ local function site_specific_packages(dev_info)
 	-- Read list of packages from site
 	site_packages = site_selections['packages']
 
-	-- Concat feature-packages with site-packages
-	local pkgs = concat_list(feature_inherited_pkgs, site_packages)
+	-- A site negation that only cancels a feature package is dropped here.
+	-- Else it reaches "apk del" for a package that was never built, and apk
+	-- then refuses all removals of the image (e.g. kmod-ath10k-ct).
+	local feature_pkg_set = {}
+	for _, pkg in ipairs(feature_inherited_pkgs) do
+		feature_pkg_set[pkg] = true
+	end
+	local pkgs = feature_inherited_pkgs
+	for _, pkg in ipairs(site_packages) do
+		local cancels_feature = string.sub(pkg, 1, 1) == '-' and feature_pkg_set[strip_neg(pkg)]
+		pkgs = append_to_list(pkgs, pkg, not cancels_feature)
+	end
 
 	-- Negations for the resulting package-list are dealt with in the calling function
 	return pkgs
-- 
2.56.1

